## Reader And Structure

Reader assumption from the assigned lesson: a Chinese-language algebra learner reading the two cube identities and their source derivation, then using the original written exercises. The text should present the identities and their argument in order without replacing the source with a new explanation or solving the exercises.

The current text serves that task. The progression is polynomial pattern, geometric-series derivation, general identity and special cases, factorization example, then cube-sum substitution. The review exercises remain in their original group rather than being moved into the main explanation. No pipeline vocabulary, new contextual facts or extra teaching material has entered the learner text.

